        {
          "dimension": "Market",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Circle faces a two-front competitive threat — Tether's entrenched dominance (70%+ share) from below and incoming bank-issued stablecoins from Bank of America, Stripe, and PayPal above, compressing USDC's addressable distribution.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "Low",
          "note": "USDC reserves are held in short-duration US Treasuries and cash equivalents managed by BlackRock, providing strong redemption liquidity under normal market conditions, though a simultaneous mass-redemption event remains a theoretical stress scenario.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Circle's Cross-Chain Transfer Protocol (CCTP) introduces smart-contract risk at every new chain integration; a bridge exploit targeting CCTP's burn-and-mint mechanism could result in unbacked USDC on destination chains.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Counterparty",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Circle's reserve concentration in a single BlackRock-managed fund and reliance on distribution partners like Coinbase and Binance creates exposure to partner-level disruptions, as illustrated when Binance ceased USDC Tron deposits.",
          "source": ""
        }
      ],
